  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Can I read fuel level remotely on a Kia Niro?",
      "a": "Yes, with a DIMO device. The DIMO LTE R1 lists fuel percentage and fuel level in liters, and AutoPi lists fuel percentage. Query the signals through the Telemetry API (GraphQL) with a Vehicle JWT."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Kia Niro with no connected services?",
      "a": "Install a DIMO device, then have the owner share the vehicle with your Developer License. Exchange your Developer JWT for a Vehicle JWT through the Token Exchange API, and read the vehicle's signals in the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Kia Niro?",
      "a": "Both DIMO device providers list idling for this model. Query the Telemetry API segments resource with the idling mechanism, which requires a DIMO device. A segment is a contiguous period where engine RPM stays in the idle range, and maxIdleRpm defaults to 1000."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Kia Niro mileage?",
      "a": "The DIMO LTE R1 device reports the odometer signal, powertrainTransmissionTravelledDistance, in km. To get a verifiable record, call the Attestation API odometer-statement endpoint (POST /v2/attestation/odometer-statement/:tokenId), then retrieve the rawVC through the Telemetry API."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect recharge sessions on a Kia Niro?",
      "a": "The DIMO LTE R1 device lists the recharge event. Use the segments resource with the recharge mechanism, which combines charging signals and state of charge. Set minIncreasePercent in the config to adjust the minimum increase, which defaults to 15."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO gives developers API access to vehicle-state data: diagnostics, fault codes, battery and fuel health, odometer, and maintenance signals. For the Kia Niro, which the record lists with ICE and EV powertrains, that data comes from a DIMO device on 2017 and newer model years. Coverage is tested, not expected. DIMO adds vehicle-state depth on top of GPS tracking; it doesn't replace it."
